# ScanGuard AI --- Container Image Vulnerability Scanner with DevSecOps Security Dashboard

> **Project status:** Sprint 4 --- Integrated security observability
> dashboard completed; dashboard cleanup and documentation in progress\
> **Current demo application:** ShopNow\
> **Next enhancements:** Multi-application support, exception
> handling/rescanning, and Claude AI security recommendations

## 1. Project Overview

ScanGuard AI is a DevSecOps security monitoring and vulnerability
reporting project designed to identify security risks before
containerized applications are promoted toward production.

The project started as a **Container Image Vulnerability Scanner with
Reporting** and has evolved into a centralized security observability
proof of concept combining container and filesystem vulnerability
scanning, secret detection, static code analysis, CI/CD pipeline
monitoring, report generation, artifact storage, Prometheus metrics, and
Grafana visualization.

The current proof of concept uses **ShopNow** as the first demo
application. The next architecture enhancement is to make application
onboarding configuration-driven so that the same platform can monitor
multiple applications.

## 2. Problem Statement

Modern containerized applications move quickly through CI/CD pipelines,
but security risks can enter through vulnerable packages and
dependencies, secrets committed to source code, static code security
issues, failed security quality gates, and inconsistent manual checks.

When Trivy, GitLeaks, SonarCloud, and CI/CD results are reviewed
separately, security visibility becomes fragmented. ScanGuard AI
consolidates these signals into a centralized DevSecOps security
dashboard.

## 3. Project Objectives

1.  Scan container images for known vulnerabilities.
2.  Scan application filesystems before container deployment.
3.  Detect accidentally committed secrets.
4.  Integrate static code analysis.
5.  Automate security checks through GitHub Actions.
6.  Generate security reports.
7.  Store reports as CI/CD artifacts for auditing and review.
8.  Export security metrics in Prometheus format.
9.  Visualize security posture in Grafana.
10. Build a foundation for multi-application monitoring.
11. Add AI-assisted security analysis as a future intelligence layer.

## 4. Current Architecture

``` text
Application Source Code
        |
        v
GitHub Repository
        |
        v
GitHub Actions
        |
        +--> GitLeaks Secret Scan
        +--> Trivy Filesystem Scan
        +--> Docker Image Builds
                    |
                    v
              Trivy Image Scan

SonarCloud --------+
Trivy Reports -----+
GitLeaks ----------+--> Python Metrics Exporter
GitHub Actions API-+    vulnerability_metrics.py
                              |
                       :8000/metrics
                              |
                              v
                         Prometheus
                              |
                              v
                           Grafana
                              |
                              v
        ScanGuard AI DevSecOps Security Dashboard
```

## 5. Technology Stack

  Tool                Purpose
  ------------------- -------------------------------------------------------------
  GitHub              Source-code repository
  GitHub Actions      CI/CD and security workflow automation
  Docker              Containerization and image builds
  Trivy               Filesystem and container image vulnerability scanning
  GitLeaks            Secret detection
  SonarCloud          Static code analysis and security quality assessment
  GitHub Artifacts    Security report storage for audit and review
  Python              Report processing, API integration, and metrics aggregation
  Prometheus          Security metrics collection
  Grafana             Centralized DevSecOps security dashboard
  PowerShell          Local and Grafana API automation
  Slack integration   Security/pipeline notification preparation

